# The icon is a byte-compared build gate. build.ps1 redraws assets\net-preset.ico
# with packaging\make_icon.py and stops the build when the SHA-256 differs, and
# .github\workflows\build.yml now runs that on a machine whose checkout nobody
# here supervises. core.autocrlf is on for this author, so what actually lands in
# a working tree is decided by git's own guess at whether a file is text. The
# guess is right today -- an .ico is full of NUL bytes within the first few
# hundred -- but nothing would notice it going wrong, and a single CRLF inserted
# into a deflate stream fails the icon check with a message about make_icon.py,
# which is the wrong place to look entirely.
*.ico binary

# The picture the README leads with. Same reason, and no gate to catch it: a
# mangled PNG just stops rendering.
*.png binary
